      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When addressing concerns regarding the Xylos win rate, it's crucial to present a multifaceted explanation that clearly illustrates the contrast between win rate and balance. Here are several points to convey:\n\n\n1. Win Rate Disaggregation: Break down the win rate by skill brackets (e.g., bronze, silver, gold, etc.) to demonstrate that while high-level players may have a favorable win rate due to being the top players, the average win rate across all players might be more representative and potentially more balanced.\n\n\n2. Matchup Analysis: Provide a holistic assessment of Xylos against a range of characters, showing that while he is strong, a specific percentage of matches may skew overall perception due to unique character matchups that favor high-level play.\n\n\n3. Pick Rate Impacts: Illustrate how Xylos' pick rate correlates with his win rate. If he is predominantly chosen by players at skill levels capable of mastering his combos, it reinforces the assumption that a subset of players is capitalizing on advanced play rather than a widespread balance issue.\n\n\n4. Technical Capabilities Comparison: Compare tech specs like cooldowns, mobility, and mobility ground games. If Xylos' stats don't deviate significantly from other viable characters, it reaffirms that",
